<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib21.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2409.12122</em>, 2024.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib22" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Yu et al. (2025)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Qiying Yu, Zheng Zhang, Ruofei Zhu, Yufeng Yuan, Xiaochen Zuo, Yu Yue, Tiantian Fan, Gaohong Liu, Lingjun Liu, Xin Liu, Haibin Lin, Zhiqi Lin, Bole Ma, Guangming Sheng, Yuxuan Tong, Chi Zhang, Mofan Zhang, Wang Zhang, Hang Zhu, Jinhua Zhu, Jiaze Chen, Jiangjie Chen, Chengyi Wang, Hongli Yu, Weinan Dai, Yuxuan Song, Xiangpeng Wei, Hao Zhou, Jingjing Liu, Wei-Ying Ma, Ya-Qin Zhang, Lin Yan, Mu Qiao, Yonghui Wu, and Mingxuan Wang.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">DAPO: an open-source LLM reinforcement learning system at scale.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib22.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CoRR</em>, abs/2503.14476, 2025.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">doi: <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_Url ltx_ref_self">10.48550/ARXIV.2503.14476</span>.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2503.14476" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2503.14476</a>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib23" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zheng et al. (2025)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Chujie Zheng, Shixuan Liu, Mingze Li, Xiong-Hui Chen, Bowen Yu, Chang Gao, Kai Dang, Yuqiong Liu, Rui Men, An Yang, Jingren Zhou, and Junyang Lin.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Group sequence policy optimization.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib23.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CoRR</em>, abs/2507.18071, 2025.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">doi: <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_Url ltx_ref_self">10.48550/ARXIV.2507.18071</span>.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2507.18071" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2507.18071</a>.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Experimental Setup for Other Baseline RL Methods</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GRPO</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">is a reinforcement learning algorithm designed to fine-tune LLMs by optimizing policies through group-based comparisons. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, we set the clipping parameter <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for the upper and lower bounds to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DAPO</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">builds upon and refines the GRPO framework, addressing key limitations such as entropy collapse and training instability. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, the lower and upper clipping thresholds were set to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{l}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{l}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{h}=0.28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{h}=0.28</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CISPO</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">lies in the direct application of a clipping mechanism to the Importance Sampling (IS) weights, as opposed to clipping the final policy update <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cui et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>. We set the clipping parameter <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for the upper and lower bounds to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GSPO</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">is a reinforcement learning algorithm developed to enhance the training stability, efficiency, and scalability of LLMs. The core of the algorithm lies in its use of a sequence-level importance ratio <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, the lower and upper clipping thresholds were set to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{l}=0.0003" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0003</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{l}=0.0003</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{h}=0.0004" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0004</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{h}=0.0004</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of the Formula for Policy Entropy Change</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Problem Setup and Assumptions</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> denote a stochastic policy parameterized by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> represents the state and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> represents an action. The policy entropy at state <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\theta}\mid s)=-\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\theta}\mid s)=-\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We make the following standard assumptions:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The policy follows a tabular softmax parameterization:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)=\frac{\exp(z_{s,a})}{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\exp(z_{s,a^{\prime}})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)=\frac{\exp(z_{s,a})}{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\exp(z_{s,a^{\prime}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{s,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{s,a}</annotation></semantics></math> are the logits corresponding to state-action pairs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Policy updates are performed using the policy gradient theorem with a sufficiently small learning rate <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, such that first-order Taylor approximations remain valid.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The advantage function <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> is baseline-centered, satisfying:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})]=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})]=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is a common practice in policy gradient methods where advantages are computed as <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s,a)-V(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s,a)-V(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to derive an approximation for the entropy change between successive policy updates:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{H}=\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\theta}^{k+1}\mid s)-\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mid s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{H}=\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\theta}^{k+1}\mid s)-\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Derivation</h4>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: First-Order Taylor Expansion of Entropy</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Treating the entropy as a function of the logits <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{s,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{s,a}</annotation></semantics></math> at a fixed state <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we employ a first-order Taylor expansion around the current parameters <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k+1}\mid s)\approx\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)+\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}(z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k+1}\mid s)\approx\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)+\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}(z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The entropy change can therefore be approximated as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}(z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}(z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Gradient of Entropy with Respect to Logits</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now compute the gradient term <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Starting from the entropy definition:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)=-\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)=-\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Following standard derivations for the softmax parameterization, we obtain:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{a}\frac{\partial\pi^{k}(a\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a^{\prime}}}(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{a}\frac{\partial\pi^{k}(a\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a^{\prime}}}(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{a}\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\left(\mathbf{1}_{a=a^{\prime}}-\pi^{k}\left(a^{\prime}\mid s\right)\right)(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{a}\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\left(\mathbf{1}_{a=a^{\prime}}-\pi^{k}\left(a^{\prime}\mid s\right)\right)(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)(\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)+1)+\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)\sum_{a}\pi(a\mid s)(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)(\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)+1)+\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)\sum_{a}\pi(a\mid s)(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Policy Gradient Update for Logits</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the policy gradient theorem and our baseline-centered advantage assumption, the logit update simplifies to:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s)}\left[\frac{\partial\log\pi_{\theta}(a^{\prime}|s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|s)}\left[\frac{\partial\log\pi_{\theta}(a^{\prime}|s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}}\left[(\mathbf{1}_{a^{\prime}=a}-\pi_{\theta}(a|s))\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}}\left[(\mathbf{1}_{a^{\prime}=a}-\pi_{\theta}(a|s))\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(a^{\prime}|s)(\mathbf{1}_{a^{\prime}=a}-\pi_{\theta}(a|s))\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(a^{\prime}|s)(\mathbf{1}_{a^{\prime}=a}-\pi_{\theta}(a|s))\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{\theta}(a|s)\hat{A}(s,a)-\pi_{\theta}(a|s)\sum_{a^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(a^{\prime}|s)\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{\theta}(a|s)\hat{A}(s,a)-\pi_{\theta}(a|s)\sum_{a^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(a^{\prime}|s)\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{\theta}(a|s)\left(\hat{A}(s,a)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}}[\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{\theta}(a|s)\left(\hat{A}(s,a)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}}[\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E19Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This follows directly from the policy gradient theorem and the baseline-centered advantage assumption <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\hat{A}(s,a^{\prime})]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: Combining the Results</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting Equations <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Step 2: Gradient of Entropy with Respect to Logits ‣ A.2.2 Derivation ‣ A.2 Proof of the Formula for Policy Entropy Change ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ CE-GPPO: Controlling Entropy via Gradient-Preserving Clipping Policy Optimization in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Step 3: Policy Gradient Update for Logits ‣ A.2.2 Derivation ‣ A.2 Proof of the Formula for Policy Entropy Change ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ CE-GPPO: Controlling Entropy via Gradient-Preserving Clipping Policy Optimization in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> into the Taylor expansion from Equation <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Step 1: First-Order Taylor Expansion of Entropy ‣ A.2.2 Derivation ‣ A.2 Proof of the Formula for Policy Entropy Change ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ CE-GPPO: Controlling Entropy via Gradient-Preserving Clipping Policy Optimization in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}(z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}(\pi^{k}\mid s)}{\partial z_{s,a}}(z^{k+1}_{s,a}-z^{k}_{s,a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E20Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\left[-\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\right)\right]\left[\eta\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\left[-\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\right)\right]\left[\eta\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Rewriting this expression as an expectation over the policy:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx-\eta\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\right)\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx-\eta\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\right)\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding the expectation:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\left(\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\left(\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E22Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">By the baseline-centered advantage assumption, the second expectation term vanishes:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\hat{A}(s,a)\right]=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\hat{A}(s,a)\right]=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the expression simplifies to:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx-\eta\left(\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\cdot 0\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx-\eta\left(\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left[\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right]-\mathbb{E}_{a^{\prime}\sim\pi^{k}}[\log\pi^{k}(a^{\prime}\mid s)]\cdot 0\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Recognizing the remaining expression as a covariance:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx-\eta\mathrm{Cov}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s),\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{H}\approx-\eta\mathrm{Cov}_{a\sim\pi^{k}}\left(\log\pi^{k}(a\mid s),\pi^{k}(a\mid s)\hat{A}(s,a)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">This completes the derivation of the desired formula.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of the Gradient of CE-GPPO Objective</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we derive the gradient of the proposed CE-GPPO loss function. Recall that the objective is defined as</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>CE-GPPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|y_{i}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\ell^{(i)}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|y_{i}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\ell^{(i)}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E26Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where}\quad\ell^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where}\quad\ell^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\beta_{1}\cdot\,\dfrac{1-\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\,\delta\,\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t},&amp;\text{if }\delta&lt;1-\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0,\\[8.0pt]
\beta_{2}\cdot\,\dfrac{1+\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\,\delta\,\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t},&amp;\text{if }\delta&gt;1+\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&gt;0,\\[8.0pt]
\delta\cdot\,\hat{A}_{i,t},&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.392em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.392em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.392em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\beta_{1}\cdot\,\dfrac{1-\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\,\delta\,\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t},&amp;\text{if }\delta&lt;1-\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0,\\[8.0pt]
\beta_{2}\cdot\,\dfrac{1+\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\,\delta\,\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t},&amp;\text{if }\delta&gt;1+\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&gt;0,\\[8.0pt]
\delta\cdot\,\hat{A}_{i,t},&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the importance sampling ratio between the updated and reference policies:</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{sg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{sg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the stop-gradient operator, ensuring that the scaling terms <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\epsilon)/\operatorname{sg}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\epsilon)/\operatorname{sg}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\epsilon)/\operatorname{sg}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\epsilon)/\operatorname{sg}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> do not propagate gradients through <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Taking the gradient of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>CE-GPPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>CE-GPPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|y_{i}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|y_{i}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now consider the three cases in the definition of <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1: <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{(i)}=\beta_{1}\cdot\frac{1-\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\cdot\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{(i)}=\beta_{1}\cdot\frac{1-\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\cdot\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{sg}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{sg}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as a constant, the gradient only flows through <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E30X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{1}\frac{(1-\epsilon)}{\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}}\cdot\frac{\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{1}\frac{(1-\epsilon)}{\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}}\cdot\frac{\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E30Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{1}\frac{(1-\epsilon)}{\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}}\cdot\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{1}\frac{(1-\epsilon)}{\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}}\cdot\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)}\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E30Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{1}(1-\epsilon)\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{1}(1-\epsilon)\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2: <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;1+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;1+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{(i)}=\beta_{2}\cdot\frac{1+\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\cdot\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{(i)}=\beta_{2}\cdot\frac{1+\epsilon}{\operatorname{sg}(\delta)}\cdot\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly,</p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}=\beta_{2}(1+\epsilon)\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}=\beta_{2}(1+\epsilon)\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 3: Otherwise.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{(i)}=\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{(i)}=\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A1.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}=\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\ell^{(i)}=\delta\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the three cases, we may summarize the gradient as:</p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E35X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>CE-GPPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{CE-GPPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|y_{i}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\mathcal{F}_{i,t}(\theta)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|y_{i}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\mathcal{F}_{i,t}(\theta)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid y_{&lt;t},x)\cdot\hat{A}_{i,t}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the weighting factor <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{i,t}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{i,t}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="A1.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{i,t}(\theta)=\begin{cases}\beta_{1}\cdot(1-\epsilon),&amp;\text{if }\delta&lt;1-\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0,\\[5.0pt]
\beta_{2}\cdot(1+\epsilon),&amp;\text{if }\delta&gt;1+\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&gt;0,\\[5.0pt]
\delta,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{i,t}(\theta)=\begin{cases}\beta_{1}\cdot(1-\epsilon),&amp;\text{if }\delta&lt;1-\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0,\\[5.0pt]
\beta_{2}\cdot(1+\epsilon),&amp;\text{if }\delta&gt;1+\epsilon\text{ and }\hat{A}_{i,t}&gt;0,\\[5.0pt]
\delta,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof.</p>
</div>
